  <h2>Short description (25 words)</h2>
  <p>Mailkin translates emails in other languages right inside Apple Mail on the Mac. Translation runs on-device with Apple's built-in engine, so emails never leave the Mac.</p>

  <h2>Long description</h2>
  <p>Apple Mail on the Mac can translate selected text, but not whole emails. Mailkin fills that gap. Once it's turned on in Mail › Settings › Extensions, every email in a language you've chosen opens already translated into your own language, with its layout, links and images intact. A banner says which language the email was in, and Show Original restores the original with one click. You can always or never translate specific senders, and choose per language whether to translate automatically, only on request, or never.</p>
  <p>Mailkin uses Apple's Translation framework, which runs on the Mac. Email content is never sent to a server, there's no account, and Mailkin never modifies the messages stored in the mailbox. It supports {{ site.languageCount }} languages, and the first {{ site.freeEmails }} translated emails are free before a one-time purchase.</p>

